    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d297">

                <pb facs="0349" n="299" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg299"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Pringle.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-02-16"><hi rendition="#italic">February 16,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 79.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I append a copy of your telegram of 8th
                    instant, reporting the statement of Mr. Peterson, consul at Tegucigalpa, that if
                    any Americans in the army of Vasquez should be captured by Bonilla they will be
                    shot.</p>
                <p>In an interview with the minister of Nicaragua, I find that Dr. Guzmán does not
                    share Mr. Peterson’s apprehensions.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
